I've decided to handle the specific error checks within `Login.tsx` itself. After examining `dbService.ts`, I'll utilize the existing `getSystemUsers` method to verify a user's existence when authentication fails. While adding a dedicated helper in `dbService` was considered for cleanliness, the simplicity and efficiency of the client-side approach make this the best choice for now. This should give the user much better feedback.


